WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.530
An AI-generated patch passed 155
selected upstream tests.

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:08.710
Independent checks still caught an
incomplete repair.

00:00:10.417 --> 00:00:14.237
The patch fixed the main Boltons
dictionary implementation, but

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.437
missed its required standalone copy.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:21.923
With empty input, that object reports
length one, while its keys

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:23.003
and items are empty.

00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:27.463
This is one genuine incomplete repair,
not a model accuracy

00:00:27.473 --> 00:00:28.163
statistic.

00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:33.623
A different retained patch fixes both
implementations and passes

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.563
both check sets.

00:00:35.113 --> 00:00:38.843
Different generation procedures mean
this is not a fair vendor

00:00:38.853 --> 00:00:39.323
comparison.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.450
Patch Audit keeps the exact change,
source identity, logs, and

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.150
expected-versus-observed evidence.

00:00:48.917 --> 00:00:52.777
Explore the public recorded showcase
without credentials. It

00:00:52.787 --> 00:00:56.417
displays historical evidence; fresh
auditing stays local.

00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:59.257
AI can write the patch. Check the
evidence.
